# Closed-Lost & Current-Customer Analysis

*Nitra internal skill documentation — converted from `closed-lost-analysis-skill.skill`*

Monthly closed-lost and current-customer analysis for Nitra, re-derived from primary sources (Sigma, Salesforce, Gong call briefs) rather than inherited spreadsheet hypotheses. Pulls the $500K+ population for a time window, resolves Salesforce IDs, fans out evidence-based extraction per deal (why it died / why it won, death moment, stall stage, reason tags, GPO channel and spend, adoption state, risk signals), scores re-engagement, and builds a formula-driven Excel workbook plus an optional deck.

Use this whenever John asks for the closed-lost analysis, loss reasons, win/loss review, churn or at-risk read on customers, GPO/purchasing-channel columns, re-engagement gameplan, or "run the monthly" — even if he doesn't say "closed lost" explicitly. Also use it when asked to refresh, redo, or extend any earlier version of this analysis.

A repeatable, evidence-first pipeline. The point of this skill is that every claim about why a deal died or how a customer is doing traces to a dated quote in Salesforce or Gong. The original monthly sheet's analyst hypotheses turned out to be wrong for 226 of 246 deals once checked against sources, so do not shortcut the primary-source pass.

