## Reference: Subagent prompt — current-customer extraction

One `general-purpose` subagent per batch, all spawned in one turn. Replace `{{BATCH}}` and `{{OUT}}`.

> Build an evidence-based profile of a set of CURRENT Nitra customers (Closed Won deals) from Salesforce primary sources including Gong call recordings/summaries.
>
> **INPUT:** `{{BATCH}}` — a JSON array with: oppId (Salesforce Opportunity Id), opportunity, accountId, account, amount, closeDate, createdDate, owner, leadSource, accountDupCount.
>
> **COMPANY CONTEXT:** Nitra sells a Visa card for independent medical practices (~2.2% cashback on medical/healthcare spend, 2% other business spend), a spend-management/AP platform (QuickBooks integration), and "NitraMart", a supply marketplace with 5-10% back on select injectables (notably Avastin). Heavily ophthalmology/retina. Competitors: Amex, Capital One, Chase, WEX, Corpay, Ramp, Bill.com/Divvy, Comdata, PNC. Purchasing channels/GPOs: Besse Medical, McKesson (incl. OnMark Vision GPO), CuraScript SD, AmerisourceBergen/Cencora, Cardinal Health, Henry Schein, Medline, Biocare, Ally GPO; Medivant, Turbare and Northmark are Avastin compounders/repackagers.
>
> **EXTRACTION** — use `mcp__cc5af9f6-21f2-4dda-afce-989ccc5c69d6__soqlQuery`:
> (a) Opportunity detail, ~12 oppIds per query:
> `SELECT Id, Name, Amount, StageName, CloseDate, CreatedDate, Description, NextStep, Owner.Name, Account.Name, AccountId FROM Opportunity WHERE Id IN ('...',...)`
> (b) Activity, 3-5 ids per query, by WhatId AND by AccountId — for won deals most post-sale conversation is logged against the account, not the opportunity:
> `SELECT WhatId, AccountId, Subject, ActivityDate, Type, Description FROM Task WHERE WhatId IN (...) ORDER BY ActivityDate DESC`
> `SELECT WhatId, AccountId, Subject, ActivityDate, Type, Description FROM Task WHERE AccountId IN (...) ORDER BY ActivityDate DESC`
> Gong records have Subjects starting "[Gong"; Descriptions contain "Call brief:", "Key Discussion Points:", "Next steps:".
>
> `Task.Description` is NOT filterable with LIKE in this org; use SOSL (`find`) for keyword searches.
>
> **CONTEXT MANAGEMENT:** Won accounts have long histories. Never pull all accounts at once. If a tool result is auto-saved to a file, use `mcp__workspace__bash` with jq/python to extract only the fields you need. Consider dumping the batch's activity to a local file once and grepping it per account.
>
> **KNOWN TRAPS:** Many 2025 opportunities were backfilled on 2025-08-30 with backdated close dates and no pre-close discovery — leave displacedCard empty rather than guessing. Records that are NOT genuine new customers appear regularly: byte-identical Pipedrive double-loads created seconds apart, underwriting-approval-only shells with $0 balances, added EINs under an existing customer, dormant never-activated logos, same-day record artifacts, accounts that asked Nitra to close. Flag these clearly in "blockers". Recurring themes worth checking for (but never assuming): Avastin price vs Northmark ~$30, Turbare exiting pre-filled syringes, McKesson ACH-only contracts, GPO pricing Nitra can't honour, QuickBooks/Sage Intacct sync failures, credit-limit ceilings, CSM handoff gaps.
>
> **FOR EACH customer produce:**
> - `account`, `oppId`, `amount` (copy from input)
> - `whyWon` — 1 sentence (max ~160 chars), the specific reason they chose Nitra, grounded in sources. Name the driver. If sources don't say: "Not evidenced in sources."
> - `displacedCard` — card/vendor Nitra displaced or supplemented. "" if unknown.
> - `competitiveSet` — other vendors evaluated, comma-separated. "" if none.
> - `gpo` — named GPO/distributor/compounder, normalized. Multiples joined " / ". "" if not named. Never a card/fintech.
> - `gpoSpend` — stated spend through that channel, unit-preserving ("$1.5M/month", "~200 Avastin syringes/week"). "" if not stated.
> - `adoptionState` — "fully ramped" | "partially adopted" | "onboarding" | "stalled/low usage" | "at risk" | "unknown", from post-close evidence.
> - `blockers` — friction limiting adoption/expansion, 1 sentence. "" if none.
> - `riskSignals` — explicit warning signs in recent activity (rate complaints, competitor pitch, champion departure, vendor friction, limit constraints, service issues), 1 sentence. "" if none.
> - `expansionAngle` — concrete, evidence-backed growth opportunity, 1 sentence. "" if none.
> - `keyContact` — named champion/DM with title if available.
> - `evidenceStrength` — "strong" | "moderate" | "weak"
> - `notableQuote` — one verbatim quote (max ~200 chars) with a date. "" if none.
>
